; 14-develop-an-unfinished-proof-safely.kurt
;
; Develop an unfinished proof safely
;
; Use `todo FORMULA` when a known gap should remain visible in the final result:

load propositional
prop A, B

show A implies B
proof
    assume A
        todo B
qed

; Use `sandbox` for experiments that must not affect the surrounding theory:

prop C, D
use C

sandbox
    use D
    D

C
expect "ProofError"
    D

; Use `break` to abandon an open block immediately -- in the `proof` of a `show`, only the proof:
; the claim stays open for a new `proof`, and a second `break` withdraws it. A sandbox is
; discarded whether it closes by a dedent or by `break`.
